# The published list of the group backends a group block runs on (GroupBackendOption): scalar_group_backend, the JVM
# scalar backend, the reference semantics of every backend (com.yang_bo.gezi.narrowblocks.groups.ScalarGroupBackend);
# jvm_array_group_backend, the JVM array backend, whose columns of row numbers are int arrays moved by generated
# kernels (com.yang_bo.gezi.narrowblocks.groups.JvmArrayGroupBackend).
# A Scott sum whose constructors are the tuple's fields, in the order of the
# enum's cases; an entry.lambdalattice imports this file and writes a
# constructor as the field backend of group_blocks_enabled, and EntryData reads
# which alternative it takes by structure
# (com.yang_bo.gezi.contest.entry.EntryData, THE OPTIONS AS SCOTT CONSTRUCTORS).
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λscalar_group_backend jvm_array_group_backend. scalar_group_backend)
λ scalar_group_backend
. (λtuple. tuple λscalar_group_backend jvm_array_group_backend. jvm_array_group_backend)
λ jvm_array_group_backend
. export scalar_group_backend jvm_array_group_backend
